## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of closures, promise sharing, and TTL eviction in a small utility.

## Key Concepts
- Closures and per-id state
- Promise deduplication for in-flight calls
- TTL-based eviction and error handling

## Code Example
```javascript
function createMemoizedAsync(fn, ttl) {
  const cache = new Map();
  return async (id) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    const entry = cache.get(id);
    if (entry && now - entry.t < ttl) return entry.p;
    const p = fn(id);
    cache.set(id, { t: now, p });
    setTimeout(() => {
      const e = cache.get(id);
      if (e && e.p === p) cache.delete(id);
    }, ttl);
    try {
      return await p;
    } catch (e) {
      cache.delete(id);
      throw e;
    }
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test TTL eviction and in-flight deduplication?
- How would you adapt for cancelable promises or revocation of in-flight calls?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of closures, Promise deduplication, request cancellation, and caching strategies in building a production-ready fetch helper. It also touches on memory management with LRU caches and handling abortable requests.

## Key Concepts
- Closures for per-key state isolation
- Promise deduplication to prevent redundant network requests
- Cancellation with AbortController for stale requests
- LRU cache implementation using Map for ordered storage
- Edge cases: rapid toggling between keys and stale data handling

## Code Example
```javascript
const api = (() => {
  const inFlight = new Map();
  const cache = new Map();
  const MAX_CACHE = 50;

  function memoFetch(key, options = {}) {
    if (cache.has(key)) {
      const entry = cache.get(key);
      cache.delete(key);
      cache.set(key, entry);
      return Promise.resolve(entry);
    }

    if (inFlight.has(key)) {
      return inFlight.get(key);
    }

    const controller = new AbortController();
    const promise = fetch(key, { ...options, signal: controller.signal })
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        inFlight.delete(key);
        if (cache.size >= MAX_CACHE) {
          const firstKey = cache.keys().next().value;
          cache.delete(firstKey);
        }
        cache.set(key, data);
        return data;
      })
      .catch(err => {
        inFlight.delete(key);
        throw err;
      });

    inFlight.set(key, { promise, controller });
    return promise;
  }

  function cancel(key) {
    if (inFlight.has(key)) {
      inFlight.get(key).controller.abort();
      inFlight.delete(key);
    }
  }

  return { memoFetch, cancel };
})();
```
